 "notes": "MERIDIAN v2 MERIDIAN SIGN (No.10, front, full body; drawn full so the same frames serve the shot-1 x3 chest-up crop and the 9b x1 bridge). Front view, never mirrored (no west strip). Registration = Stand Front: body centre x 64, soles on row 102, contact = [64, 102] (centre between the planted boots; contactL / contactR = the outer row-102 sole pixels, soleL / soleR = sole centres); the feet rows 92-102 are pixel-identical on all six frames, the hips pop 1-3 px toward screen-right above them. The sign arm is his LEFT arm (screen-right, the friend side; lead decision, PLAN.md 4.1). fingertip = the index tip, one rising-then-falling arc MS1 (70,30) -> MS2 (83,14) -> MS3 (87,7) -> MS3b (105,14) -> MS4/MS4b (113,33); eye = the tapped eye (his left = screen-right; the needle pupil / needle's-eye iris anchor: OPEN on MS4 (75,25)); eyeL / eyeR = screen-left / screen-right eye; fist = the sign hand's knuckle block; head = skull centre; pelvis = hip centre (popped). Points are pixel indices (studioAnim adds 0.5; contact lands on the bottom edge of row 102). bbox = [x0,y0,x1,y1] measured on the art. Shot 1 (x3 crop): MS1 0.00-0.30, MS2 0.30-0.40, MS3 0.40-0.57, MS3b 0.57-0.74, MS4 0.74-1.05, MS4b 1.05-1.15 (the blink), MS4 1.15-1.40 (eyes OPEN under the needle's-eye iris push 1.22-1.40: the brief's \"MS4b 1.05\" returns to MS4 by 1.15). Shot 9b (x1): Run -> Point P1 1.34 (turn-in bridge) -> MS1 1.40 -> MS3 1.52 -> (MS3b 1.59) -> MS4 1.66 -> MS4b 1.98 -> MS4 2.10-2.30. Studio layer: Art only (numbers in Art; no Num/Ball layer). The ball is never drawn in a frame: the game draws it at ball/boot/forehead. Studio: Sochetra / MeridianSign / Front (Side/Back views blank).",
